4. Implications
Friction is added exactly where you want it. Improving a shared template now requires a deliberate session with the fence lowered — a build agent can never do it as a side effect of "fixing" one video. That's the point, but it means legitimate template work has one extra step.
Builders lose template choice; you gain reproducibility. The same lesson always produces the same plan, which means plans become testable (Phase-4-style mutations apply to the planner too) and a bad plan is a bug you fix once, not a taste incident you catch per video.
The design-contract table becomes data. The prose table either gets generated from the lookup or annotated as its mirror — otherwise you've recreated the doc-drift problem you just spent a build fixing.
Existing workspaces are unaffected. The beat_type field applies to new builds; the 13 mid-career workspaces finish under the current contract (the fence and integrity manifest protect them immediately, though).
Honest limit: "certainty of no violations" is achievable for every encoded rule. What stays probabilistic is taste you haven't encoded yet — that's what the pilot gate and the two vision lanes are for, and B6 is the mechanism that drains that category to empty over 2–3 batches.
